# =============================================================================
# .dockerignore — SETU Docker build context filter
# =============================================================================
# Exclude everything from the Docker build context except the minimal set of
# files the webhook server needs. This keeps `docker build` fast and prevents
# accidental inclusion of the massive LangBot web/ directory, venvs, caches.
#
# Note: The compose.yml mounts ./plugins as a volume at runtime, so the
# Dockerfile only needs webhook_server.py and requirements.txt baked in for
# standalone runs. The COPY in Dockerfile.webhook ensures these exist even
# without the volume mount.
# =============================================================================

# Deny everything first
*

# Then allow-list what we need (parent dirs must be included for nesting)
!webhook_server.py
!plugins/
!plugins/seva_memory/
!plugins/seva_memory/**
